// SandboxControlService is the orchestrator-side control plane for
// `daft-sandboxd serve`. A sandbox-host opens a single outbound
// mTLS connection to the orchestrator and:
//
//   1. calls RegisterSandbox with its host-resource advertisement,
//      holding the server-streamed channel open for the lifetime
//      of the sandboxd process. The first event is a SubscriptionReady;
//      Slice A4 will reuse the stream for orchestrator → sandboxd
//      Dispatch.
//   2. emits Heartbeat unaries on a fixed interval so the
//      orchestrator's registry can mark sandboxes dead when the
//      heartbeats stop.
//
// Caller identity for every RPC is the mTLS leaf-cert fingerprint
// surfaced via withPeerMiddleware — there is no sandbox_id field;
// the sandboxd's own identity is the identifier.
//
// See PLAN.md "Direction (2026-05-12)" Phase A.

